ars from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids January to February and September to October each came in under 90% of normal in 36 of those years. In 2025, November to December finished at 40% of normal on the middle. So far in 2026, February to March and March to April each sat at 59% of normal on the middle. Every grid had its driest year in 2007, with grid 17281 down at 53%.</p>"}
